set.body:
Produce a short, decision-ready product PRD for the first executable Sherlock recall-to-video vertical. This is separate from bd-01M1EA8J4KFQRHZ5SF326B6WFZ, which governs construction integrity.

User constraint: Sherlock-derived data may be stored/shared; raw video files may not be stored or shared. AMR runtime use is authorized. The PRD must preserve that boundary: raw video is an external pinned dependency/reference only.

The first honest path is: admitted Sherlock source/annotation bundle plus recall transcript -> witnessed baseline construction family -> explicitly qualified fixed RecallGraph view -> existing sparse nomination and GraphHsmm posterior P/transition flow F/signature -> durable serialized result -> locally inspectable markup/visualization.

Required decisions and acceptance:
- define input/output/partial/refusal states and their provenance/identity;
- distinguish annotation/repaired coordinates from pinned media PTS and refuse exact playback claims until a checked crosswalk exists;
- expose segmentation/interpretation conditioning and retained alternatives; baseline must not render as calibrated science;
- define family/search receipts, fixed-view projection receipt/loss, and binding of downstream results to the complete construction/source identity;
- define a minimal terminal command and visualization showing cells, overlapping claim supports, alternative constructions, source/external posterior mass, transition flow, authority, coordinate basis, and sensitivity;
- state the dependency sequence and exact proof gates across B0R bd-01M1CQ5YS5M25F7HD9NN5YVAYP, C1, D0/D1A/D1B, V1, and the output/visual slice;
- separate usable diagnostic vertical from later calibration/empirical claims;
- use role names/descriptive placeholders where public Scala vocabulary or a module/ADR is not yet authorized;
- include a concrete definition of done and one representative user journey, without implementing code.

Exact path for this bead: docs/plans/2026-09-01-sherlock-recall-product-prd.md only. Before editing, claim/begin and reserve that path. Gate: exact-path diff-check, self-contained symbol/reference scan, byte count and SHA-256 publication, independent product/science review. No Scala/source edits, raw video ingestion, corpus redistribution, ADR decision, public vocabulary approval, candidate authorization, landing, or closure.
